  <div class="section-title">
    CLIENT AUTHORIZATION SOURCE DOCUMENT MUST BE ATTACHED TO REQUEST.
  </div>

  <div class="sub-section">
    Each Sender Authorization Process Type will require a BIC, DN or ID
  </div>

  <div class="sub-section">
    <b>BIC Address</b> – The BIC address must be present on the Swift table, except for TRDS. Trade Authorization must be entered manually by the user.
  </div>

  <ul class="rules">
    <li><b>COLC</b> - Allow movement of cash (collateral) from segregated account to head account</li>
    <li><b>COLS</b> - Allow movement of shares (collateral) from segregated account to head account</li>
    <li><b>DNPF</b> - Do Not Allow MT304 Forward (AFWD) Processing</li>
    <li><b>DNPA</b> - Do Not Allow MT304 Spot (ASET) Processing</li>
    <li><b>FWDP</b> - Allow MT304 Forward (AFWD) Processing</li>
    <li><b>PBAM</b> - Payment Based Allocation Method</li>
    <li class="sub-note">CSG & TAX must ensure Momentum profile is created for successful execution</li>
    <li><b>PMTS</b> - Payment Authorization</li>
    <li><b>TRDS</b> - Trades Authorization Custody / MX20022 Mutual Funds FTP</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="sub-section">
    <b>MX20022 Mutual Fund Distinguished Name (DN)</b>
  </div>
  <div class="description">
    MFDN - Distinguished Names that are authorized to instruct trades for Mutual Funds MX20022 Messaging.
  </div>

  <div class="sub-section">
    <b>ACH Identification Number (ID)</b> - users must provide up to 18 characters.
  </div>

  <div class="description">
    ACHD – ACH Debit Blocking (ID) - Important: Removal of ACHD linkage from a blocked account to itself is strictly prohibited.
  </div>

